      <!-- Section 4: Sensitivity Math & eDPI -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          4. Sensitivity Mathematics: The Universal eDPI & cm/360 Guide
        </h2>
        <p>
          Comparing raw in-game sensitivity sliders across different games is mathematically misleading because each game engine uses different angular yaw constants. The only two standardized metrics for cross-game calibration are <strong>eDPI (effective Dots Per Inch)</strong> and <strong>cm/360 (physical distance required for a complete 360° camera rotation)</strong>:
        </p>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-zinc-900 text-zinc-100 font-mono text-xs overflow-x-auto my-4 border border-zinc-800">
          <code>eDPI = Mouse Hardware DPI × In-Game Sensitivity Slider Value</code><br />
          <code>cm/360 = (360 / (DPI × In-Game Sensitivity × Engine Yaw Constant)) × 2.54</code>
        </div>

